Match the Suunto DM4 stylesheet on a namespace declaration.

`test_xslt_transforms()` picks its stylesheet by root element plus, for the two
ambiguous roots, the presence of an attribute:

	{ "Dive", "SuuntoDM4.xslt", "xmlns" },
	{ "Dive", "shearwater.xslt", "version" },

The "xmlns" test is made with xmlGetProp(), but libxml2 does not keep namespace
declarations in a node's property list - they live in `nsDef`. xmlGetProp()
therefore returns NULL for "xmlns" on every document, so the Suunto DM4 entry
can never match: a Suunto DM4 dive export (root <Dive xmlns="http://schemas.
datacontract.org/2004/07/Suunto.Diving.Dal">, e.g. dives/Dive_2013-02-02-1614.xml)
falls through the table untransformed and parses to zero dives. Running the same
file through xsltproc with SuuntoDM4.xslt produces the expected divelog, so the
stylesheet is fine and only the dispatch is wrong.

Look at nsDef when the attribute being tested is "xmlns". Shearwater XML has no
default namespace, so the two entries stay distinguishable.

Report upstream and drop this patch when the pin carries a fix.

--- a/core/parse-xml.cpp
+++ b/core/parse-xml.cpp
@@ -1819,11 +1819,20 @@
 			if (info->attribute == NULL)
 				break;
 
-			xmlChar *prop = xmlGetProp(root_element, (const xmlChar *)info->attribute);
-			if (prop != NULL) {
-				xmlFree(prop);
+			/* libxml2 keeps namespace declarations in nsDef, not in
+			 * the property list, so xmlGetProp() never reports an
+			 * "xmlns" attribute - the Suunto DM4 entry above would
+			 * never match. */
+			if (strcmp(info->attribute, "xmlns") == 0) {
+				if (root_element->nsDef != NULL)
+					break;
+			} else {
+				xmlChar *prop = xmlGetProp(root_element, (const xmlChar *)info->attribute);
+				if (prop != NULL) {
+					xmlFree(prop);
 
-				break;
+					break;
+				}
 			}
 		}
 		info++;
